From 3e6f01049555b3fb7e33a051a1d30374440fb27c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] input_origin: room plumbing (not hidden) is agent;
 forward origin to compute-host turns

Follow-up to #1797 review nits (t_01a1d271c47294ad):

1. pending_hidden was transient (popped once session_workdir marks the row hidden), so only the
   first submit into a hidden session classified 'agent'. Treating every persisted hidden row as
   'agent' instead would be wrong: Bot Mode's canonical "Bot Chat" is born hidden and David types
   into it (canonical-chat.ts), so his bot DMs would stop stamping last-human-input and read as agent
   to pre_llm_call plugins. Hidden is no authorship signal. input_origin now keys on Bot Mode room
   plumbing instead, consistently for every submit: the live session's room_plumbing flag, or (for a
   resumed session with no flag) its stored row (model_config.room_plumbing, or a hidden "Group:" row:
   the rule agent_factory._stored_session_runtime_overrides applies on resume, mirrored in
   human_input to leave that upstream function untouched). The row is read only for a would-be human
   submit with a session key; an unreadable store falls back to 'human'.
2. The compute-host isolated dispatch now pops the stashed _submit_input_origin and forwards it:
   _submit_prompt_to_compute_host(input_origin=) -> turn.start frame "input_origin" ->
   ComputeHost._run_real_turn -> _run_prompt_submit(input_origin=). A failed dispatch hands the
   stash back so the inline fallback's _run_after_agent_ready still reads it. An older child
   ignores the extra frame key.
3. note_submit's docstring lists every non-stamping case (agent transport, agent_created, room
   plumbing, relayed/hosted params, hidden widget intents, cross-session sends, no request id).

Proof: RED on origin/main (8 failed: stored plumbing rows 'human', pending_hidden 'agent', no
input_origin kwarg/frame key, remote turn origin ''); GREEN 54 tests in the 2 files; 54 files
touching these seams 1330 passed / 8 skipped; 18/18 mutants killed; scripts/check health ok.
Replay: worker-1 profile DBs hold 0 hidden/room-plumbing rows (Desktop Bot Mode rows live on the Macs).
